  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1035 PM MDT Wed Jun 10 2026\n\nUpper level high pressure will continue to control our weather on\nThursday and into Friday. Thursday will be dry with wide spread\n100+ degree high temperatures across the lowlands. A trickle of \nmoisture will try to slip into the area on Friday, but the rain \nchances will be limited to locations east of the Rio Grande. The \nridge aloft will be weaker but still an influence, so it will be a\nchallenge to get more than just a few thunderstorms going Friday \nafternoon and evening. \n\nFor Saturday through Monday, the upper level ridge will drop to\nour southwest and that will allow a little more moisture to get \ninto the area. It won't be a lot of moisture, especially on \nSaturday so rain showers and thunderstorms will struggle. High \ntemperatures those days will be near seasonal averages, which will\nkeep most lowland locations just shy of the triple digit mark. It\nlooks like the extended models build the upper level ridge back \ninto New Mexico for the middle of next week. This ridge position \nwill dry us out and heat us back up with temperatures once again \nabove 100 across much of the lowlands.",
